From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 16:25:48 +0200
Subject: PCI: intel-gw: allow building on MIPS

The Intel Gateway PCIe controller is a DesignWare core behind an Intel
application-logic wrapper, and the same wrapper sits in front of the
three root complexes on the Lantiq/Intel GRX500 family (xRX500, GRX350),
which are MIPS interAptiv rather than x86. The register block matches:
the application block's CCR/LTSSM, MSG_CR, PMC, IRNEN and IRNCR live at
the same offsets, and the port logic registers are the stock DesignWare
ones.

Nothing in the driver is x86-specific -- it is written against readl(),
the DesignWare core library, the generic clock, reset, phy and gpiod
APIs, and device properties. The dependency simply predates any non-x86
user.

Widen it rather than replace it, so the existing Intel Gateway (LGM)
platforms keep the driver exactly as before, and COMPILE_TEST coverage
on every other architecture stays in place.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/Kconfig b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/Kconfig
index 349d4657393c..d59b3eefccdc 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/Kconfig
@@ -175,7 +175,7 @@ config PCIE_HISI_STB
 
 config PCIE_INTEL_GW
 	bool "Intel Gateway PCIe controller "
-	depends on OF && (X86 || COMPILE_TEST)
+	depends on OF && (X86 || MIPS || COMPILE_TEST)
 	depends on PCI_MSI
 	select PCIE_DW_HOST
 	help
